    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I've noticed that when they're working hard, they make this really distinct high-pitched whistling or whining sound. Is there a specific mechanical reason for that noise during the boost phase?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sound primarily comes from air being compressed and forced through the turbocharger's waste gate and any associated intake piping as the impeller spins faster under load. If the turbo is properly sized for your engine's demand, you should hear more of a smooth whoosh rather than a high-pitched whistling note, whereas a high-pitched whine often indicates the turbine is hovering just above the surge or churn point on its curve, regulating flow to the intake. Proper tuning of the compressor and wastegate ensures the air pressure rises smoothly without causing the aerodynamic turbulence that generates that specific noise.",
